  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "In triangle \\(ABC\\) the ratio \\(AC:CB\\) is \\(3:4.\\) The bisector of the exterior angle at \\(C\\) intersects \\(BA\\) extended at \\(P\\) (\\(A\\) is between \\(P\\) and \\(B\\)). The ratio \\(PA:AB\\) is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(1:3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(3:4\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(4:3\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(3:1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(7:1\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1961-p31.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The exterior angle bisector theorem gives \\[ \\frac{PA}{PB}=\\frac{AC}{CB}=\\frac34. \\] Since \\(PB=PA+AB,\\) write \\(PA=3t,\\) \\(PB=4t.\\) Then \\(AB=t,\\) so \\(PA:AB=3:1.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Apply the exterior angle bisector theorem to the full lengths \\(PA\\) and \\(PB\\)",
        "Use \\(PB=PA+AB\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
